### 4 Features not tested

Exclude payment, shipping, university SSO, SMS/email delivery and third-party cloud internals because they are outside the release. Observe the deployed provider through health and TLS checks; do not claim to certify its infrastructure. A mocked active-exchange guard in Sprint 1 does not replace Sprint 2 real-database integration testing.


## 5 Test approach and strategy

Unit: deterministic hashing/token/rate-limit, validation, score and transition functions. Integration: FastAPI with an isolated PostgreSQL database and real migrations/constraints. System: browser register -> login -> create -> search -> edit -> delete, then request -> match -> exchange -> return. Acceptance: teammate checks SRS criteria on the deployed build and records evidence. Regression: all relevant automated tests on every PR, full suite on main before demo.


### 5.1 Security validation

Verify credential redaction, token tampering/expiry/logout, ownership bypass, profile privilege escalation, SQL injection handling, throttling, TLS and contact privacy. Use synthetic accounts. Test the API directly so a hidden UI control cannot conceal a server authorization defect. Restrict load and negative tests to team-owned test environments.


### 5.2 Entry and exit

Entry: requirement and API baselines available, test environment and synthetic data ready, migrations pass, selected feature build available. Exit: 100% planned in-scope cases executed, all high-priority criteria passed, no critical/high unresolved defects, required CI green, coverage thresholds met, reviewed PR merged and evidence linked. Performance thresholds require recorded measurements; an unrun test cannot be waived by changing the RTM to A.


### 5.3 Test isolation and concurrency

Use independent test database/schema and reset fixtures per test. Inject a controllable clock for JWT expiry and rate-limit windows. Verify race tests with separate DB sessions and synchronization; a serial unit test cannot prove locking. Never seed or reset production data as part of CI.


