### 10 Risks and mitigation

Late shared scaffold delays dependent work: use contract fixtures, then rerun against real endpoints. Missing domain or hosting settings block acceptance: record B with owner. In-memory limiter and mocked exchange checks limit realism: document and retest. Free-host cold starts distort load results: publish both cold and warm behavior. Keep test accounts/data isolated.


### 11 Assumptions and dependencies

The team supplies university domains, account identities and accessible hosting. Sprint 2 details are reviewed on 2 November. The TA spreadsheet link is pending; it affects submission tracking but not test design. Test IDs from the supplied plan are preserved and additional cases fill coverage gaps.


### 12 Suspension and resumption

Suspend affected tests if the environment is unavailable for more than four hours, data integrity is compromised or blockers prevent >30% of planned cases. Continue independent tests where possible. Resume after environment/data recovery, blocker fix and smoke tests; rerun affected cases on the new commit.


